<p class="mb-3">
  <%= link_to "← All sensors", admin_climate_sensors_path, class: "text-sm text-primary underline" %>
</p>

<%= render CardComponent.new(title: "Which reading matches the device?") do %>
  <p class="text-gray-700">
    Govee's API does not document whether it reports temperature in Celsius or Fahrenheit, and for
    these sensors it is often Fahrenheit even when the app shows Celsius. Reading it wrong would
    store years of unusable history, so it is confirmed once, by hand, against the device itself.
  </p>

  <p class="text-gray-700">
    Govee reports <strong class="text-xl"><%= number_with_precision(@raw, precision: 1) %></strong>
    for <strong><%= @sensor.display_name %></strong> right now.
    Open the Govee app (or look at the sensor's own display) and see which of these it agrees with.
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 my-4">
    <div class="rounded border border-gray-200 p-4 text-center">
      <p class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-1"><%= number_with_precision(@as_celsius, precision: 1) %> °C</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-3">if the API reports Celsius</p>
      <%= button_to "It says about #{number_with_precision(@as_celsius, precision: 0)} °C",
                    admin_climate_sensor_path(@sensor),
                    method: :patch,
                    params: { climate_sensor: { temperature_unit: Climate::Sensor::UNIT_CELSIUS } },
                    class: btn_classes(:primary) %>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded border border-gray-200 p-4 text-center">
      <p class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-1"><%= number_with_precision(@as_fahrenheit, precision: 1) %> °C</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-3">if the API reports Fahrenheit</p>
      <%= button_to "It says about #{number_with_precision(@as_fahrenheit, precision: 0)} °C",
                    admin_climate_sensor_path(@sensor),
                    method: :patch,
                    params: { climate_sensor: { temperature_unit: Climate::Sensor::UNIT_FAHRENHEIT } },
                    class: btn_classes(:primary) %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-0">
    Picking the wrong one is recoverable: every reading stores the raw number Govee sent alongside
    the converted value, so the history can be recomputed. Come back here and choose again.
  </p>
<% end %>
